    {
      "id": "dfbd0db5-11dc-4a24-9a71-56b5b52947a4",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        -288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 536,
        "height": 692,
        "content": "## Turn whiteboard photos into meeting notes and action items with Gemini\n\n### How it works\nThe meeting ends, someone photographs the whiteboard, and the notes never get written. Submit the photo through the built-in n8n form and a Basic LLM Chain with Google Gemini reads the handwriting directly from the image, returning a summary, the decisions taken, every action item with its owner and due date, and any open questions. The meeting is logged to Google Sheets, the notes are emailed to all attendees, and when action items exist they are split out and appended one row each to an Action Items sheet you can sort and filter. If the photo is unreadable the submitter gets an email asking for a clearer shot.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Google Sheets and Gmail.\n2. Point the two Sheets nodes at your spreadsheet (tabs: Meetings, Action Items).\n3. Open the form URL on your phone and submit a whiteboard photo.\n\n### Customization tips\nSwap the Action Items sheet for Notion or Trello, or add a Slack post for the team channel."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
